A written explanation of how Python's import system connects main.py to utils.py.
Python allows me to use functions from one file in another by using imports. In this project, I created `utils.py` to store useful functions such as `square()`, `is_even()`, and `celsius_to_fahrenheit()`.
In `main.py`, I used `from utils import square, is_even, celsius_to_fahrenheit` to bring these functions into the program. Since both files are in the same `src` folder, Python can find `utils.py` easily.
This makes the project cleaner and easier to manage because I can reuse the functions in `main.py` without writing the same code again. It also saves time and makes the code easier to understand and maintain.
